WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.532 --> 00:00:03.309
- [Anuar] The humpback
whale, they're huge.

00:00:03.309 --> 00:00:05.865
It's like seeing a bus in the water.

00:00:05.865 --> 00:00:08.563
And she looks at you with those big eyes,

00:00:08.563 --> 00:00:09.844
and she stares at you,

00:00:09.844 --> 00:00:12.170
it feels beautiful.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:15.817
And that's when you know
that she's letting you in.

00:00:15.817 --> 00:00:17.596
- [Female Narrator] That's Anuar Patjane.

00:00:17.596 --> 00:00:19.274
He's a photographer.

00:00:19.274 --> 00:00:21.916
And in 2015 he won the grand prize in

00:00:21.916 --> 00:00:25.180
National Geographic's
Traveler Photo contest

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:28.605
for his photo "Whale Whisperer."

00:00:28.605 --> 00:00:31.052
So we're talking about
what it feels like to come

00:00:31.052 --> 00:00:35.219
face to face with one of the
largest mammals on our planet.

00:00:37.141 --> 00:00:39.777
- [Anuar] The first time,
it was in Roca Partida.

00:00:39.777 --> 00:00:41.042
We knew we were gonna see the whales

00:00:41.042 --> 00:00:43.102
because we were hearing them.

00:00:43.102 --> 00:00:46.021
And when they are nearby,
your whole body resonates.

00:00:46.021 --> 00:00:47.271
It's so strong.

00:00:48.565 --> 00:00:50.821
I love the sound of the whales.

00:00:50.821 --> 00:00:53.595
It's as beautiful as seeing them.

00:00:53.595 --> 00:00:54.902
- [Female Narrator] He's underwater.

00:00:54.902 --> 00:00:56.550
And off in the distance...

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.796
- [Anuar] I saw the
silhouette of the whale.

00:00:58.796 --> 00:01:00.276
(whale noise)
Big, big silhouette that looks

00:01:00.276 --> 00:01:02.177
like a submarine without features.

00:01:02.177 --> 00:01:03.734
It's like a big object.

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:05.213
- [Female Narrator] And as he got closer,

00:01:05.213 --> 00:01:06.591
things became clearer.

00:01:06.591 --> 00:01:08.892
- [Anuar] Oh, there's
the eye, there's the fin.

00:01:08.892 --> 00:01:12.856
Oh, that's a big whale.
It's a very big whale.

00:01:12.856 --> 00:01:14.866
- [Female Narrator] The
most profound feeling he had

00:01:14.866 --> 00:01:17.705
was a connection to the whale herself.

00:01:17.705 --> 00:01:20.375
- [Anuar] She looks at
you. Right into your eyes.

00:01:20.375 --> 00:01:21.947
And you feel the connection.

00:01:21.947 --> 00:01:23.960
It is a mammal connection.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.460
You feel accepted.

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:29.739
- [Female Narrator] Anuar's
been diving for 17 years.

00:01:29.739 --> 00:01:32.876
And his photographs are
more than just pictures.

00:01:32.876 --> 00:01:35.124
- [Anuar] Most of the photos
I make, I try to share them.

00:01:35.124 --> 00:01:38.191
Because people that doesn't
dive and doesn't know the ocean,

00:01:38.191 --> 00:01:41.889
they might start to pay
attention to the ocean.

00:01:41.889 --> 00:01:43.247
And I like whales.

00:01:43.247 --> 00:01:44.679
It's a reminder

00:01:44.679 --> 00:01:46.588
that we share the world with

00:01:46.588 --> 00:01:50.638
very, very wise and
beautiful animals down there.

00:01:50.638 --> 00:01:53.221
(Whale sounds)

